# 6. Core Capability Areas

These capability areas define the scope and positioning of GPL Software Services.

They are reference material for topic planning and factual accuracy and do **not** all need to appear in individual articles.

Specific responsibilities depend on the client engagement and project scope.

## 6.1 Implementation and Configuration

GPL Software Services helps organizations implement and configure production workflow systems around real operating requirements.

GPL's public positioning includes end-to-end implementation and configuration of Autodesk Flow Production Tracking and related production tools.

This capability may involve:

* platform setup
* workflow mapping
* configuration
* permissions and process alignment
* adapting systems to production structure
* implementation planning around active work

The important editorial point is the relationship between configuration and the workflow it supports, not the number of configuration options available.

## 6.2 Customization

Production platforms often require adjustment before they fully support the operating model of the organization using them.

GPL Software Services can customize and extend production tools so that software behavior better reflects production requirements.

Customization may involve:

* workflow logic
* fields and statuses
* task behavior
* interfaces
* process-specific functionality
* extensions to standard platform behavior

Articles should use specific customization examples only when they materially support the argument.

## 6.3 Workflow Automation

GPL Software Services includes workflow automation designed to reduce repetitive production work and unnecessary manual coordination.

Automation may support areas such as:

* repetitive production actions
* recurring handoffs
* process triggers
* file or status-related workflows
* production coordination

The value of automation should be evaluated through the specific workflow problem it addresses.

Do not automatically frame automation as beneficial simply because a manual process exists.

## 6.4 Tool Integrations

GPL Software Services connects production systems when information or workflow actions need to move between platforms.

GPL's public Software Services positioning includes integrations between Autodesk Flow and systems such as Perforce, Jira, and third-party file-sharing tools.

This capability can also be understood more broadly through:

* production-system interoperability
* API integrations
* connected workflow systems
* cleaner system handoffs
* reduced dependence on manual information transfer

Do not turn integration articles into catalogs of connected applications.

The editorial focus should remain on what the relationship between systems changes operationally.

## 6.5 Support, Documentation, and Training

Software implementation continues after the technical configuration is complete.

GPL's Software Services positioning includes support, documentation, and user training as organizations adopt and evolve production systems.

This may involve:

* documentation
* onboarding
* process guidance
* user training
* post-launch refinement
* ongoing support

These areas should be discussed when adoption or long-term support is relevant to the article rather than added automatically to every Software Services discussion.

## 6.6 Iteration and Workflow Evolution

Software Services is not limited to initial deployment.

Production systems may need to change as workflows, teams, tools, or production requirements evolve.

GPL's public positioning includes ongoing workflow optimization and iteration, making long-term system evolution an important part of the business unit.

This supports GPL's positioning as a continuing workflow partner rather than a one-time implementation provider.

