# 9. Relationship to Other GPL Business Units

## 9.1 Software Services vs Managed Services

Managed Services focuses on the ongoing stability, support, and operational state of the technology environment.

Software Services focuses on the software and workflow systems operating inside that environment.

A useful distinction is:

* Managed Services supports the environment in which production operates.
* Software Services improves how production software and workflow systems function within that environment.

Avoid turning Software Services articles into general infrastructure-support discussions unless infrastructure directly affects the software or workflow problem being examined.

## 9.2 Software Services vs Security & Compliance

Security & Compliance focuses on security risk, content protection, access governance, compliance frameworks, and security controls.

Software Services can work inside secure production environments and may need to account for permissions, access, or security requirements during implementation, but security governance is not its primary role.

If the central argument concerns security exposure, compliance readiness, identity governance, or content protection, the article likely belongs to Security & Compliance.

## 9.3 Software Services vs Consulting

Consulting is primarily advisory and strategic.

Software Services is execution-oriented.

It helps organizations implement, configure, customize, connect, support, and evolve the systems that production teams actually use.

## 9.4 Software Services as a Bridge Layer

Software Services often sits between technical infrastructure and day-to-day production operations.

It is the point where systems, workflow logic, and users interact.

This makes the business unit particularly relevant when the underlying technology environment is functional but the workflow around it remains difficult to operate, maintain, or scale.

